1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,041
The most famous car in cinema was

2
00:00:02,041 --> 00:00:03,773
not built the way you think.

3
00:00:03,953 --> 00:00:07,164
The original script gave Bond's Aston Martin

4
00:00:07,164 --> 00:00:08,550
only a smokescreen.

5
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:12,028
The ejector seat was a compressed-air mock-up.

6
00:00:12,208 --> 00:00:14,807
The headlights that blind Bond in the

7
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:17,687
film are reflections from a giant mirror.

8
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:19,729
And the car that started it all

9
00:00:19,729 --> 00:00:22,430
has been missing since nineteen ninety-seven.

10
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:26,335
Two secrets hidden inside the Aston Martin

11
00:00:26,335 --> 00:00:28,996
DB5, with every claim sourced.

12
00:00:29,345 --> 00:00:32,750
Our sources are Wikipedia's DB5 page,

13
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:35,787
Top Gear, the James Bond Dossier,

14
00:00:35,787 --> 00:00:39,744
the Ecurie article on the Thunderball cars,

15
00:00:39,744 --> 00:00:41,768
Carole Nash, NBC News,

16
00:00:41,768 --> 00:00:43,701
CNN, Old Cars Weekly,

17
00:00:43,701 --> 00:00:47,658
InsideHook, an RM Sotheby's catalogue and a

18
00:00:47,658 --> 00:00:50,510
travel-site specification page.

19
00:00:50,690 --> 00:00:52,419
They disagree in places,

20
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:54,580
and we show the disagreements.

21
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:57,163
Our own arithmetic is labelled.

22
00:00:57,513 --> 00:00:58,512
Secret one.

23
00:00:58,692 --> 00:01:01,979
The Bond Dossier says the initial Goldfinger

24
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:04,892
script gave the DB5 only a smokescreen.

25
00:01:05,072 --> 00:01:06,381
The rest, the guns,

26
00:01:06,381 --> 00:01:08,517
the slashers, the ejector seat,

27
00:01:08,517 --> 00:01:10,377
grew out of the production.

28
00:01:10,557 --> 00:01:13,836
Top Gear says production designer Ken Adam

29
00:01:13,836 --> 00:01:16,801
sketched the car and discussed it with

30
00:01:16,801 --> 00:01:19,845
special effects supervisor John Stears.

31
00:01:20,025 --> 00:01:22,458
So the legend started as a single

32
00:01:22,458 --> 00:01:24,449
gadget and then multiplied.

33
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:26,900
Where did the ideas come from?

34
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:30,355
Top Gear quotes Adam saying his frustration

35
00:01:30,355 --> 00:01:33,174
with parking damage to his own Jaguar

36
00:01:33,174 --> 00:01:34,849
influenced the design,

37
00:01:34,849 --> 00:01:38,125
including rear guns and bumpers that became

38
00:01:38,125 --> 00:01:39,572
like boxing gloves.

39
00:01:39,752 --> 00:01:42,806
The Bond Dossier says director Guy Hamilton

40
00:01:42,806 --> 00:01:46,499
proposed the revolving number plates after receiving

41
00:01:46,499 --> 00:01:47,635
parking tickets.

42
00:01:47,815 --> 00:01:50,707
Two gadgets, according to these sources,

43
00:01:50,707 --> 00:01:52,587
came from parking trouble.

44
00:01:52,937 --> 00:01:55,904
The Bond Dossier says the tyre slashers

45
00:01:55,904 --> 00:01:58,947
were inspired by the scythed chariots in

46
00:01:58,947 --> 00:01:59,555
Ben-Hur.

47
00:01:59,735 --> 00:02:02,852
Carole Nash says Stears took inspiration for

48
00:02:02,852 --> 00:02:05,757
the machine guns and the bulletproof rear

49
00:02:05,757 --> 00:02:08,095
screen from the wings of a Second

50
00:02:08,095 --> 00:02:09,441
World War Spitfire.

51
00:02:09,621 --> 00:02:12,733
These are the sources' accounts of inspiration.

52
00:02:12,913 --> 00:02:15,321
We have no production notes of our

53
00:02:15,321 --> 00:02:16,738
own to confirm them,

54
00:02:16,738 --> 00:02:18,509
so we attribute each one.

55
00:02:18,858 --> 00:02:21,400
The full gadget list in the Bond

56
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,338
Dossier: a homer that tracks a target

57
00:02:24,338 --> 00:02:25,846
on a hidden screen,

58
00:02:25,846 --> 00:02:29,499
extending front bumpers that Adam designed but

59
00:02:29,499 --> 00:02:31,643
were never shown on screen,

60
00:02:31,643 --> 00:02:33,946
tyre slashers, a smokescreen,

61
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:34,978
an oil slick,

62
00:02:34,978 --> 00:02:36,646
a bulletproof screen,

63
00:02:36,646 --> 00:02:38,552
revolving number plates,

64
00:02:38,552 --> 00:02:41,649
an ejector seat and front machine guns.

65
00:02:41,829 --> 00:02:42,657
By our count,

66
00:02:42,657 --> 00:02:43,867
that is nine items,

67
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:45,969
and one of them never appeared in

68
00:02:45,969 --> 00:02:46,542
the film.

69
00:02:46,892 --> 00:02:49,365
The oil slick had an earlier idea.

70
00:02:49,545 --> 00:02:52,292
The Bond Dossier says dropping nails was

71
00:02:52,292 --> 00:02:54,763
abandoned because it was too easy to

72
00:02:54,763 --> 00:02:55,107
copy.

73
00:02:55,287 --> 00:02:56,190
In the film,

74
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:58,447
according to the same article,

75
00:02:58,447 --> 00:03:01,382
the oil slick sends a pursuing Mercedes

76
00:03:01,382 --> 00:03:02,360
over a cliff,

77
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:05,671
and the smokescreen blinds another Mercedes,

78
00:03:05,671 --> 00:03:07,628
which crashes into a tree.

79
00:03:07,808 --> 00:03:10,116
We take the article's word for what

80
00:03:10,116 --> 00:03:11,105
the film shows.

81
00:03:11,455 --> 00:03:13,197
Now the ejector seat.

82
00:03:13,377 --> 00:03:15,829
The Bond Dossier says Adam stated the

83
00:03:15,829 --> 00:03:18,083
device came from a jet fighter and

84
00:03:18,083 --> 00:03:19,475
was fully functional,

85
00:03:19,475 --> 00:03:22,723
though the filming used a compressed-air mock-up.

86
00:03:22,903 --> 00:03:24,709
So the seat in the film was

87
00:03:24,709 --> 00:03:25,980
not the real thing.

88
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,937
Those two statements sit side by side

89
00:03:28,937 --> 00:03:30,063
in the article,

90
00:03:30,063 --> 00:03:31,489
and we report both.

91
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:34,900
Whether a working seat was ever installed

92
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,265
is not settled by our sources.

93
00:03:37,614 --> 00:03:40,041
The machine guns have their own secret.

94
00:03:40,221 --> 00:03:42,605
The Bond Dossier says they fire from

95
00:03:42,605 --> 00:03:44,062
behind the headlights,

96
00:03:44,062 --> 00:03:46,247
but the lights that blind Bond in

97
00:03:46,247 --> 00:03:48,697
the film are reflections from a giant

98
00:03:48,697 --> 00:03:49,161
mirror.

99
00:03:49,341 --> 00:03:51,350
It is a piece of film trickery

100
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:53,091
rather than a car feature.

101
00:03:53,271 --> 00:03:55,732
Top Gear scored the DB5 ten out

102
00:03:55,732 --> 00:03:57,241
of ten for gadgets,

103
00:03:57,241 --> 00:03:59,782
which is its opinion of the car,

104
00:03:59,782 --> 00:04:01,212
not a measurement.

105
00:04:01,561 --> 00:04:03,767
How long did the conversion take?

106
00:04:03,947 --> 00:04:06,891
Top Gear says a small team converted

107
00:04:06,891 --> 00:04:08,608
the car in six weeks,

108
00:04:08,608 --> 00:04:12,942
using pneumatics, hydraulics and acetylene and oxygen

109
00:04:12,942 --> 00:04:13,433
tanks.

110
00:04:13,613 --> 00:04:15,884
A crew member had to squeeze into

111
00:04:15,884 --> 00:04:18,431
the boot to trigger the smoke screen.

112
00:04:18,611 --> 00:04:22,020
The Bond Dossier also says Stears tricked

113
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:24,265
out the car over six weeks.

114
00:04:24,445 --> 00:04:26,546
Two sources, one figure.

115
00:04:26,896 --> 00:04:30,256
The Ecurie article lists the gadgets fitted

116
00:04:30,256 --> 00:04:31,975
to the first Bond car:

117
00:04:31,975 --> 00:04:35,179
hydraulic over-rider rams front and rear,

118
00:04:35,179 --> 00:04:38,695
a Browning thirty-calibre machine gun in each

119
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:41,665
front wing, tyre slashers in the wheel

120
00:04:41,665 --> 00:04:44,165
hubs, a retractable rear screen,

121
00:04:44,165 --> 00:04:46,900
a radar-tracking scope in the dash,

122
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,385
dispensers for oil,

123
00:04:48,385 --> 00:04:49,869
caltrops and smoke,

124
00:04:49,869 --> 00:04:53,229
revolving plates and an ejection system for

125
00:04:53,229 --> 00:04:54,714
the passenger seat.

126
00:04:55,063 --> 00:04:57,807
Ecurie adds two things fitted but not

127
00:04:57,807 --> 00:04:58,919
used on screen:

128
00:04:58,919 --> 00:05:01,588
a driver's door telephone to MI6 and

129
00:05:01,588 --> 00:05:05,072
a hidden weapons compartment under the driver's

130
00:05:05,072 --> 00:05:05,443
seat.

131
00:05:05,623 --> 00:05:08,591
It also says the first car's gadgets

132
00:05:08,591 --> 00:05:11,394
were basic, built only to work for

133
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,136
one take.

134
00:05:12,316 --> 00:05:14,359
So the legendary car was,

135
00:05:14,359 --> 00:05:15,830
in its first form,

136
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:18,609
a film prop designed to work once.

137
00:05:18,958 --> 00:05:22,235
Even the Carole Nash article mentions that

138
00:05:22,235 --> 00:05:23,171
a stunt car,

139
00:05:23,171 --> 00:05:24,810
labelled FMP seven B,

140
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:27,697
had its German ZF gearbox fail during

141
00:05:27,697 --> 00:05:29,491
filming in Switzerland,

142
00:05:29,491 --> 00:05:32,144
so it was useless for a high-speed

143
00:05:32,144 --> 00:05:32,612
chase.

144
00:05:32,792 --> 00:05:34,983
The car the film made famous was

145
00:05:34,983 --> 00:05:37,653
therefore supported by a stunt car with

146
00:05:37,653 --> 00:05:38,817
a broken gearbox.

147
00:05:38,997 --> 00:05:40,887
That is one article's account,

148
00:05:40,887 --> 00:05:43,092
and the other sources do not repeat

149
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:43,281
it.

150
00:05:43,631 --> 00:05:46,731
Secret two is about the cars themselves.

151
00:05:46,911 --> 00:05:49,106
Most people picture one DB5.

152
00:05:49,286 --> 00:05:52,596
Wikipedia says four were made for Goldfinger:

153
00:05:52,596 --> 00:05:54,877
two used in filming and two for

154
00:05:54,877 --> 00:05:55,613
promotion.

155
00:05:55,793 --> 00:05:59,536
Ecurie says Eon wanted two near-identical cars,

156
00:05:59,536 --> 00:06:02,164
a lightweight stunt car and a car

157
00:06:02,164 --> 00:06:05,429
with Stears' gadgetry for interior shots.

158
00:06:05,609 --> 00:06:07,949
The number depends on whether you count

159
00:06:07,949 --> 00:06:09,208
the Thunderball cars.

160
00:06:09,558 --> 00:06:12,244
The first Bond car was a DB5

161
00:06:12,244 --> 00:06:16,657
prototype, chassis prefix DP slash two sixteen

162
00:06:16,657 --> 00:06:20,493
slash one, finished in Snow Shadow Grey,

163
00:06:20,493 --> 00:06:21,644
says Ecurie.

164
00:06:21,824 --> 00:06:24,526
Wikipedia says it was Dubonnet Red,

165
00:06:24,526 --> 00:06:27,537
fitted with gadgets and later stripped.

166
00:06:27,717 --> 00:06:29,737
Those descriptions conflict.

167
00:06:29,917 --> 00:06:32,106
We show both and do not decide

168
00:06:32,106 --> 00:06:33,201
which is right,

169
00:06:33,201 --> 00:06:36,267
since neither source gives a photograph or

170
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:37,289
a build sheet.

171
00:06:37,638 --> 00:06:40,541
Wikipedia says that car later appeared in

172
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:43,514
The Cannonball Run in nineteen eighty-one,

173
00:06:43,514 --> 00:06:46,346
and was stolen in nineteen ninety-seven.

174
00:06:46,526 --> 00:06:48,696
It says the car was reported missing

175
00:06:48,696 --> 00:06:49,962
in twenty twenty-one.

176
00:06:50,142 --> 00:06:52,364
Carole Nash says it was stolen in

177
00:06:52,364 --> 00:06:54,586
Florida in nineteen ninety-seven,

178
00:06:54,586 --> 00:06:57,211
after being stripped of its gadgets and

179
00:06:57,211 --> 00:07:00,847
sold, with later owners fitting non-original weaponry.

180
00:07:01,027 --> 00:07:04,022
NBC says many believe it was destroyed.

181
00:07:04,372 --> 00:07:05,684
By our arithmetic,

182
00:07:05,684 --> 00:07:08,599
the car has been missing for twenty-nine

183
00:07:08,599 --> 00:07:10,202
years as of this year,

184
00:07:10,202 --> 00:07:13,335
nineteen ninety-seven to twenty twenty-six.

185
00:07:13,515 --> 00:07:14,777
It was the original,

186
00:07:14,777 --> 00:07:16,480
the car that Connery drove,

187
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:18,625
if the sources are right about its

188
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:19,193
identity.

189
00:07:19,373 --> 00:07:21,343
Whether it is still out there is

190
00:07:21,343 --> 00:07:23,312
something no source can tell us,

191
00:07:23,312 --> 00:07:24,667
and we will not guess.

192
00:07:25,016 --> 00:07:27,524
A second car adds a twist.

193
00:07:27,704 --> 00:07:31,634
Wikipedia says filming car DB5 slash fourteen

194
00:07:31,634 --> 00:07:35,127
eighty-six slash R had no gadgets during

195
00:07:35,127 --> 00:07:35,912
shooting.

196
00:07:36,092 --> 00:07:39,231
Gadgets were added afterwards for promotion,

197
00:07:39,231 --> 00:07:41,300
and it sold at RM Auctions in

198
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,939
twenty ten for four point six million

199
00:07:43,939 --> 00:07:44,510
dollars.

200
00:07:44,690 --> 00:07:47,719
Ecurie says it was originally unmodified and

201
00:07:47,719 --> 00:07:49,647
had the gadgets added later.

202
00:07:49,827 --> 00:07:52,255
So the car many remember as the

203
00:07:52,255 --> 00:07:54,370
Bond car was a plain car in

204
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:55,075
the film.

205
00:07:55,424 --> 00:07:57,699
The price of that sale is itself

206
00:07:57,699 --> 00:07:58,339
disputed.

207
00:07:58,519 --> 00:08:02,419
Wikipedia and InsideHook say four point six

208
00:08:02,419 --> 00:08:03,871
million dollars.

209
00:08:04,051 --> 00:08:07,106
NBC News reported two point six million

210
00:08:07,106 --> 00:08:10,396
pounds, or four point one million dollars,

211
00:08:10,396 --> 00:08:11,649
at RM in London,

212
00:08:11,649 --> 00:08:14,313
with an estimate above three and a

213
00:08:14,313 --> 00:08:15,879
half million pounds,

214
00:08:15,879 --> 00:08:18,308
bought by Harry Yeaggy of Ohio.

215
00:08:18,488 --> 00:08:19,859
By our arithmetic,

216
00:08:19,859 --> 00:08:22,296
the gap is about eleven percent.

217
00:08:22,645 --> 00:08:25,297
NBC describes the car as silver,

218
00:08:25,297 --> 00:08:28,776
first driven by Sean Connery in Goldfinger

219
00:08:28,776 --> 00:08:31,179
and also used in Thunderball.

220
00:08:31,359 --> 00:08:33,287
It says the car came with a

221
00:08:33,287 --> 00:08:36,286
